  "clarifications": {
    "c0": "C0 is reported as a contrast like C1-C3 (coverage of its true difference, resolutions, wrong signs); P4 is not evaluable as recorded, because the two RF fits use different training label draws (seeds 2027 and 2028), so conditional on the fitted models their true difference is not zero (truth, deviation c0_not_null). Its CR2 and DeLong rejection rates are reported descriptively only.",
    "s_star": "s* = 1.25: the mean ratio over C1-C3 was 6.26 at s_u = 1.25 and 4.73 at 1.00, at distances 0.76 and 0.77 from 5.5, equal within Monte Carlo error (the calibration grid is non-monotonic by up to 1.0 between neighbouring values; one training draw, 200 test draws per value). 1.25 was taken by the recorded rule (closest) and gives a mean ratio inside the v1 range 4.4-6.6.",
    "prevalence": "The record fixes no prevalence; the population of the 39 blocks has the prevalence of the reference (truth), 0.37-0.39.",
    "small_tests": "Step 4 draws, per scenario, from one generator with seed 3002 (restarted for each scenario): 19 block indices with replacement, then cell effects and labels of those cells. Each appearance of a block is its own cluster. Draws with a single class would be skipped and counted (none expected).",
    "decisions": "Resolved: 95 % interval excludes 0. Wrong sign: resolved with the sign opposite to the true difference. Coverage: the interval contains the true difference of the truth file. CR2 without the floor rule (the record names CR2 only). Empirical MDE: 2.80 x SD of the 2,000 small-test estimates. P2, P3 and P6 are evaluated on the declared contrasts C1-C3; P5 on those of C1-C3 within the margin (wrong-sign part: all of C1-C3).",
    "small_test_ratio": "Added after scoring, as a clarification of the explanation (not of any result): the median SE_CR2/SE_DeLong ratio of the small tests (1.1-2.7) is below the 4.4-6.6 of v1 and the 6.26 of the calibration mainly because of cell size, not the number of clusters: the 39 blocks of 10-60 rows have a median of 27 rows, against about 56 per cell in the 182 test cells of the calibration, and the design effect grows with the rows per cell. S2 matches the dependence of v1 on whole test cells, not the ratio of the small tests."
  },
